<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I101c478c0f27f9fd444ccd4699a5c94e76d3b17e" commit="e13815a0e83d01c1dd62f2afcca2fe507ce92857" commit_message="[autotest] Store afe_host in and remove host attributes to/from machine dict.  There are multiple times when the AFE is queried for random bits of info (host attibutes, labels, etc).  To reduce the number of calls, store the AFE host object into the machine dict so we can store it into the host class. I chose the AbstractSSHHost class to grab it out of the arg dict since that is used both by CrosHost and ADBHost.  Also removed host attributes as a class instance attribute since afe_host contains all that info already.  Also use the os labels to do host class detection.  BUG=chromium:546741 TEST=Tested a couple scenarios: - Manually on moblab to make sure cros/adb/testbed devices all pass   dummy tests. - Trybot job on gnawty-paladin. - Moblab dummy suite run to ensure no breaking backward compatibility changes   (moblab on R52 and testing with a tryjob gnawty build). - test_{that,droid}.py on a cros/adbhost device.  Change-Id: I101c478c0f27f9fd444ccd4699a5c94e76d3b17e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349990 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="349990" owner_email="kevcheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="18" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/90/349990/18" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ida6fde3fe043118ed76d895477888a7b66161745" commit="acf282baded6d5066581b5c2f678e643beeb5acd" commit_message="[autotest] Update cros board label to not update itself.  Only generate the board label if the host does not have the board label, otherwise just the existing board label.  BUG=chromium:624207 TEST=locally using contrib/print_host_labels.py CQ-DEPEND=CL:349990  Change-Id: Ida6fde3fe043118ed76d895477888a7b66161745 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358501 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358501" owner_email="kevcheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/01/358501/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic60a8bc1d84c4f9a7b5664e9daddfa331b6a890c" commit="ff003ef11831827cbb1d257f767c4575be2bb95a" commit_message="reef: Fix board ID ADC scaling factors  The ADC multiplier and divider factors were lazily set to 1 when the board support was first added, so the value was not scaled properly.  The conversion formula is: Vi = CHNnDAT * (Vfs / 1024) where Vfs = Vref = 2.816V for Reef.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=added debug print and reading now approximately matches what the voltmeter reads.  Change-Id: Ic60a8bc1d84c4f9a7b5664e9daddfa331b6a890c Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358613 Reviewed-by: Kevin K Wong &lt;kevin.k.wong@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358613" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/13/358613/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia091fbbad7ffce2da9a04c48c7676ad9b4a08dea" commit="13e67bd03e904f55e20b06eb2acc0f488ee7d5bc" commit_message="reef: Update board ID values and add positive error margin  This makes corrections to the board ID values and also adds a small multiplier to allow for higher-than-ideal voltages to match.  Currently we see values that are below the ideal value by about 2.5%, so it seems like a good idea to also allow slightly above ideal voltage to account for variations in Vref or PP3300_EC that could cause the calculated value to become higher than expected.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=none  Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Ia091fbbad7ffce2da9a04c48c7676ad9b4a08dea Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358614 Reviewed-by: Kevin K Wong &lt;kevin.k.wong@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358614" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/14/358614/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I3d62fab09f679ae6460f2bb2104ad9ef4fabef7b" commit="3d279b3af8211a7af572df254b9a6d6e6eedad1a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/tegra: Calculate HDA audio values  Calculate and program CTS/N/AVAL audio values with given pixel clock.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54787 TEST=Hear HDMI audio working.  Change-Id: I3d62fab09f679ae6460f2bb2104ad9ef4fabef7b Signed-off-by: David Ung &lt;davidu@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358510 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358510" owner_email="davidu@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/10/358510/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie311c3f871ba642ee984e6be3fd2c4e2c370c343" commit="44e8cd1b6a9ae944fec203cba5f52c352c541007" commit_message="sysroot_wrapper: Wunused-local-typedefs is now supported by clang.  This flag is now supported by clang. Need to update the wrapper to avoid removing it when the user has specified it.  BUG=chromium:625067 TEST=Built Simple Chrome with GN and Clang compiler by default.  Change-Id: Ie311c3f871ba642ee984e6be3fd2c4e2c370c343 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358770 Commit-Ready: Luis Lozano &lt;llozano@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Luis Lozano &lt;llozano@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Steven Bennetts &lt;stevenjb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358770" owner_email="llozano@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/70/358770/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic62b9fc9825de371fcb78a307686bdc933f883df" commit="6be1a421e351c942a47998a803c5d003c2ceebfe" commit_message="chaos: Reduce schedule to 2 DUTs and 2 securities.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: Ic62b9fc9825de371fcb78a307686bdc933f883df Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358179 Commit-Ready: Tien Chang &lt;tienchang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Tien Chang &lt;tienchang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bindu Mahadev &lt;bmahadev@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="358179" owner_email="tienchang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/79/358179/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icfe234465c9bdcf1151f83f9b68f4362ecca0bed" commit="0c59688cb2b9c333c13b53c23dca5c4c5acfb204" commit_message="Updating kernel version for some boards  Updating expected kernel versions for platform_KernelVersionByBoard test  BUG=chromium:626109 TEST=ran the test on lab elm machine  Change-Id: Icfe234465c9bdcf1151f83f9b68f4362ecca0bed Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358383 Commit-Ready: Pramod Bathini &lt;pbathini@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Pramod Bathini &lt;pbathini@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Katherine Threlkeld &lt;kathrelkeld@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="358383" owner_email="pbathini@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/83/358383/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4aa549145ad724368290ea7566ca41577d92194b" commit="207ae7564a6f94d7bf6991d7ab1de29f5ab24a9d" commit_message="autotest: record logs after forcing reset when repairing  If the DUT was no longer accessible through SSH, ensure we are recording the logs after re-gaining SSH access (e.g. after trigger a servo reset) before clobbering them.  BUG=chromium:615662 TEST=run a local autoserv instance: sudo ./server/autoserv -R ...  Change-Id: I4aa549145ad724368290ea7566ca41577d92194b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/355739 Commit-Ready: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="355739" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/39/355739/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I937afeaa8ff5f976724bd3e528bc16166aab4026" commit="0c4b09de48847c18fe62afe783ffde077d2981c5" commit_message="Upload CTS test results to seperate GS buckets.  Parse keyval to get build info and parent_job_id. Add build info, parent_job_id and job_id to timestamp.zip gs path. Add job_id to result.xml.gz gs path.  BUG=chromium:619209 TEST=manually run gs_offl